ew and far between they're not  making policy they are you know when you  talk about tuition free college paid out  of taxes where people who get really  rich from their businesses pay more  that's a capitalist thing that happens  in socialism you wouldn't have those  ultra rich people except when the  socialist state is a corrupt state in  which case you wouldn't that happens but  then they probably wouldn't be paying  high taxes single-payer healthcare is a  capitalist idea where the fruits of  capitalism are used to make sure  everyone has health care regardless of  whether they can personally afford it  based on the job that they have they are  setting up this fake enemy of socialism  when they are really fighting more  progressive capitalists that's really  the majority of what the the ideas are  that they claim to be fighting as far  left it's total cringe but the really  scary thing about this the thing that is  depressing is that in a lot of parts of  the country this stuff probably is  appealing I understand that as someone  who lives in Massachusetts I laugh when  I see stuff like this but because it  seems almost like a parody but there are  parts of the  country where folks like these could  actually win and we need to be  activating and organizing against them  because otherwise they will win and even  if it's a fake war against socialism  that they think they're waging they can  still be successful as long as they  prevent serious progressive reforms from  actually taking place so I know that we  laugh it off in a lot of parts of the  country and we joke in this is a Fox  News echo chamber these folks are never  going to get elected nobody's going to  fall for the false the the straw men  that they are putting together that's  not true in a lot of parts of the  country this stuff resonates and sadly I  mean even here in Massachusetts in some  of the more rural parts you see a  sympathy for this type of ideology so  we've got to fight every district we'